  "certificate_sha256": "fcb5b0374c1ee68b32193491dcb1d905a7ac39ef61e7c56a7bbfe6bf6b56d23c",
  "claim": "The ordinary-polytopal H9/14 record 35 cannot be the nerve of a compact hyperbolic Coxeter polytope.  Exhausting the 420 labelled order-five Lanner placements on each of three common-core missing faces leaves no elliptic completion at the rank-nine vertices. The all-right shadow obstruction is monotone under every possible additional non-right finite Coxeter label.",
  "kind": "h9_14_record35_compact_coxeter_label_obstruction",
  "proof": {
    "compact_inputs": [
      "each order-five minimal nonface supports a Lanner diagram",
      "each rank-nine vertex diagram is elliptic",
      "the classical order-five Lanner table has 420 labelled placements"
    ],
    "exact_reduction": "For the supports {0,5,7,9,10}, {1,5,7,9,10}, and {4,5,7,9,10}, join the placement tables on their common four-node core.  Twelve rank-five restrictions leave 96 states.  Under S3 x S4 these form orbits of sizes 24 and 72; rank-six restrictions exhibit affine D4+A1 and affine D5.",
    "monotone_shadow_lemma": "For normalized Coxeter Gram G=I-A, A is symmetric and entrywise nonnegative.  Ellipticity is lambda_max(A)<1. Changing an external m=2 entry to any m>=3 increases A entrywise, hence cannot decrease lambda_max by the Perron-Frobenius monotonicity theorem.  Therefore no extra non-right labels can repair the certified non-elliptic principal subdiagram."
  },
